{"title":"2025 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Anna has a three term arithmetic sequence of integers. She divides each term of her sequence by a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />, and tells Bob that the three resulting remainders are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1d1611143f5792dc0f61f3b130af88cb790c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, in some order. For how many values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is it possible for Bob to uniquely determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1d1611143f5792dc0f61f3b130af88cb790c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are (in some order) the terms of an arithmetic sequence, then it is impossible for Bob to uniquely determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, as the terms of Anna's arithmetic sequence could be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1d1611143f5792dc0f61f3b130af88cb790c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> could be arbitarily large. Henceforth, we assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/8/f587e5ac4e92336dda55717e4b91e30a00f4218b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R \\ne 36,84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> (trivally, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2a1a90540e8e0af9c0cfc689befb54882ac027f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = -12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> case is a non-issue).\n</p><p>Suppose that the terms of Anna's sequence are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, in that order, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the remainders when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, respectively. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/e/d6e16780c9405ac52f7a4c2d7c23993dd716f3db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(20,52,R)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" /> is a permutation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c73ed093cc73a8d9a14185fa525e7067e5c3725d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />. Note that we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c2ef9ab7f200f92a033cf3fe774ec78db0c321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-x \\equiv z-y \\pmod{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"183\" height=\"20\" />, which is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb716c8d2268e25b45ad8fd494ed7a9785f20e3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x-2y+z|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e5ec9ea2c5501d738a1e079957f3ca7ad0bb342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le x,y,z &lt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/4/0d44cba52b2c001fb0352a605a771d135f79f9f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x-2y+z| \\le \\max\\{x+z, 2y\\} &lt; 2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"284\" height=\"20\" />. Furthermore, we cannot have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/c/b2cee8fe07629ea510677f1a2026e7c02da492e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x-2y+z| = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" />, as this would imply that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are in arithmetic progression. Thus, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/c/f8c5055127c79509e37e12e7e69e64c63394a54e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x-2y+z| = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Now, the key is to rephrase the condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eecb75edec0da0ccb1c8a3d0933b9d618e0b9ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = |x-2y+z|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" /> in terms of the three inequalities <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7c73e96e435f9cbfdd270dbfc1e387968e240da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = |x-2y+z| &gt; x, y, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"199\" height=\"20\" />. There are two possibilities here; either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/3/3c3b159cdce0575307cd96f4c52946b5f70da23d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+z &gt; 2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" /> (implying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/385f05887f4b7e440c6ce384679d25d5bb75d6d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=x-2y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" />) or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/3/b3340da3d22c27174be63018de3c303e6ca20660.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y &gt; x+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" /> (implying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/0/0c06c29337d682647448f48e2260fca0ed314b3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2y-x-z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" />). We handle each case separately.\n</p><p><b>Possibility 1:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/3/3c3b159cdce0575307cd96f4c52946b5f70da23d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+z &gt; 2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" />. The three inequalities <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/962dfd38fb8c4b08bded8bc1e6f81d10c1aee235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" /> become:\n</p>\n<ul>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/228650f95da86608fda62c53212a92dc3648e709.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z &gt; 2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />;</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cc20961b75672746d9722c618a1638a0f04c874.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+z &gt; 3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" />;</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b8561c287d6f0955f34e678b0fee54c5c42aeeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Notice that these inequalities are equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b55d046a2e13250bd73526127bf0fd9828c0935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,z &gt; 2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" />, as this condition implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfaac2c511bff5b6d039c4334a8c21a76e1d2220.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+z &gt; 2y+2y \\ge 3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"17\" />. Also, crucially, observe that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b55d046a2e13250bd73526127bf0fd9828c0935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,z &gt; 2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" />, without knowing anything about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we can say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/2/cc2d684d8af1c87109e8dc88918d5c73b2f6129f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = x-2y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/3/3c3b159cdce0575307cd96f4c52946b5f70da23d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+z &gt; 2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p><b>Possibility 2:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/3/b3340da3d22c27174be63018de3c303e6ca20660.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y &gt; x+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" />. The three inequalities in question become:\n</p>\n<ul>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/5/1b544ae760f0b34521c3cd8c345e55c6d86552f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y &gt; 2x+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" />;</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e339c5e9d4aa47fad29b05412029bb5bab836f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &gt; x+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" />;</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/c/82c9bdbbae6e92d04dc91e65d08f8f1c392fc61e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y&gt;x+2z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" />.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These inequalities together are equivalent to the single condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e339c5e9d4aa47fad29b05412029bb5bab836f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &gt; x+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" />, as from this we can derive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55db458f3bfdc784a67df1e111b4aa014ec55ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y &gt; 2x+2z \\ge 2x+z, x+2z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"239\" height=\"17\" />. Similarly to the previous case, we make the observation that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e339c5e9d4aa47fad29b05412029bb5bab836f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &gt; x+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" />, without knowing anything about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we can say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42ff5e800ad31914661266e90a67a7b14ae07bd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2y-x-z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/3/b3340da3d22c27174be63018de3c303e6ca20660.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y &gt; x+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, we have just demonstrated the existence of the follwing two pairs of equivalent statements: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/2/cc2d684d8af1c87109e8dc88918d5c73b2f6129f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = x-2y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b55d046a2e13250bd73526127bf0fd9828c0935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,z &gt; 2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42ff5e800ad31914661266e90a67a7b14ae07bd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2y-x-z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e339c5e9d4aa47fad29b05412029bb5bab836f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &gt; x+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1d1611143f5792dc0f61f3b130af88cb790c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in increasing order. From what we have just shown, we know that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/2/17272e6b7303cee43b02395d75dec1bf1447d342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v,w &gt; 2u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/c/80cbce0b94f39c69dd3dd34cb0da031f626d4e13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w &gt; u+v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> (possibly both). We seek to characterize when Bob is able to uniquely determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/2/17272e6b7303cee43b02395d75dec1bf1447d342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v,w &gt; 2u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> holds but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/c/80cbce0b94f39c69dd3dd34cb0da031f626d4e13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w &gt; u+v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> does not, Bob can uniquely determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f684d21d13b89ddb624be7bf1e344d6f1bebdaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v-2u+w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />. Similarly, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/c/80cbce0b94f39c69dd3dd34cb0da031f626d4e13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w &gt; u+v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> holds but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/2/17272e6b7303cee43b02395d75dec1bf1447d342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v,w &gt; 2u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> does not, Bob can uniquely determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/0/0901e36bd7072447d9d920d5f30df50d58ab078b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2w-u-v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />. However, if both the conditions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acdc24eb08045d0a9af06fe5861f4b36b320d99f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v,w&gt;2u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/c/80cbce0b94f39c69dd3dd34cb0da031f626d4e13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w &gt; u+v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> hold, it is possible for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> to equal either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f15dce79439d6e76c86e50b6ce0bef0ec7e8c6cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u-2v+w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/0/0901e36bd7072447d9d920d5f30df50d58ab078b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2w-u-v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />. For Bob to be able to uniquely determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, these values must be equal, implying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/190feab040d602473916a63772028fd81e97eeb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u-2v+w=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"122\" height=\"15\" />. However, this is impossible because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be in arithmetic progression.\n</p><p>Hence, Bob can uniquely determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> if and only if exactly one of the two conditions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7dfcd2289b78302a2588efe0e0d0ecad9d8093d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2u&lt;v,w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa83c05016f7c53e7299f847e7d7866b840621b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u+v&lt;w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> holds. All that remains is to count the number of possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, which we do by casework.\n</p><p><i>Case 1:</i> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d1999cd4a64cd6cde9443e0d93fd145a75f5266c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le R &lt; 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />. In this case, we always have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/5/d45f9c7490ed6668bc98b684f04d3323a2799af3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R + 20 &lt; 52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/0/640716285c3a225168477ace79c3a8fcb487c1ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2R &lt; 52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" />, so we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/5987680fbf87fd68916ca07cd6655d32eea741e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2R \\ge 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in this case.\n</p><p><i>Case 2:</i> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/e/e5ed1e4488cad98f7a13228593499c08c3b13e8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\le R &lt; 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" />. In this case, we always have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/3/b536b314649172c8f1a4909e6028d732cc6f3700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R+20 &lt; 52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2a435cd389369771e943b052d3e7674e5de476.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(20) \\ge R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> can be anything in this case's range. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in this case.\n</p><p><i>Case 3:</i> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/e/c1e6634e9fd615a6238cab42bc5ff6ea4e434723.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32\\le R &lt; 52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" />. In this case, we always have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66c5bb49efab0c961633e8eec6ddafb868af5d86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R+20\\ge 52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/4/bf4adaf3608deccdbc9a46953fe7212be6fcf8be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(20)&lt; 52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"20\" />, so we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/dafb1e3e6c4eebe1c80b0e9bb6b13f6778d97d51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(20) &lt; R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in this case.\n</p><p><i>Case 4:</i> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/3/c137ee6a086ed80cb36dfd7d8d7edb42c09495a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52\\le R \\le 72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" />. In this case, we always have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/f/cff9e2393694347b7515003e84a6b05df86afad7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20+52\\ge R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/3/f73c7e5aae067c718b178ae0eefb0ffb86f77b8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(20) &lt; 52, R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> can be anything in this case's range. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in this case.\n</p><p><i>Case 5:</i> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/1/a11acd6168a60c6b105de73c2f9c73b6fa1dcceb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72 &lt; R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />. In this case, we always have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/2/d623647e562faa94737d73de555e14644c665554.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20+52&lt; R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/3/f73c7e5aae067c718b178ae0eefb0ffb86f77b8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(20) &lt; 52, R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />, so there are no possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in this case.\n</p><p>This exhausts all possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa8c6955148e1a5e86b2c85e755aa0c20590c0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10+12+11+21+0 = \\boxed{54}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"226\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Sedro\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017223144\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.041 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 416/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function cou